-- title:
--   Base change pushes Haar on GL₂(L⊗_KA_K) to adelic Haar
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, and endow $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$, where $\mathbb{A}_K$ denotes the adele ring of $K$, with the Borel $\sigma$-algebra [`AutomorphicForm.glBorelOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L57) generated by its topology. Let $\mu$ be a measure on this group for that $\sigma$-algebra which is a Haar measure in Mathlib's sense (left invariant, finite on compacts, positive on open sets). The assertion is the existence of a real number $c_\mu>0$ such that for *every* function $F\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)\to\mathbb{C}$ — with no measurability or integrability hypothesis, the Bochner integral being $0$ by convention when the integrand fails to be integrable — one has $$\int F(\mathrm{bc}(x))\,\mathrm{d}\mu(x)=c_\mu\int F(g)\,\mathrm{d}\,\mathtt{adelicGLHaar}(g).$$ Here $\mathrm{bc}=$ [`AutomorphicForm.baseChangeGL K L`](def/AutomorphicForm_BaseChangePlaces.html#L69) is the group homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ obtained by applying, entrywise, the ring isomorphism `baseChangeEquiv` $\colon L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathbb{A}_L$ (the commutativity isomorphism of the tensor product followed by the comparison isomorphism between $L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K$ and the adele ring of $L$), and `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` is Mathlib's Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra `glBorel`. The constant $c_\mu$ is uniform in $F$.
--
--   This is the measure-theoretic normalisation step accompanying adelic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: uniqueness of Haar measure turns an arbitrary Haar measure upstairs into a positive multiple of the chosen adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, with one constant serving all integrands. It supplies the proportionality datum used in the estimate [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure) for twisted orbital integrals over double cosets.
